1
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:38,920
ADAPTED FROM <i>THE EARLY SPRING</i> ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:22,400
LOVE BEGINS ON A BITTERSWEET NOTE

4
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:32,120
Why the long face? It's longer
than the filefish we serve here.

5
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:34,840
Anyone who saw you
would think I'd served you fake liquor.

6
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:36,480
- Save it.
- Drink with me.

7
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:44,920
Trouble in love?

8
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,320
As if.

9
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:56,480
I guessed it, didn't I? So you're dating?

10
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,720
We are,

11
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,640
but we're keeping it secret.

12
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:02,280
A secret relationship?

13
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:03,760
It feels strange.

14
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:08,880
Ms. Shang is a great girl.

15
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:11,920
She's kind, hardworking, and dependable.

16
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,760
And she looks at you

17
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:16,040
like an adoring little fawn.

18
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,440
What's not to like?

19
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:19,760
You should at least make it official.

20
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:22,360
You think I wanted to keep it secret?

21
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:26,200
Whenever she sees me in public,
she avoids me like the plague,

22
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,440
terrified someone might notice.

23
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:32,640
And the two of us
can only see each other on weekends.

24
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:34,080
Is that a normal relationship?

25
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:36,600
It is a little unusual,

26
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:39,280
but I can understand why.

27
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:42,440
Ms. Shang has a strong sense of pride.

28
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:44,320
She's afraid you'll look down on her

29
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:47,920
and that your relationship
won't survive once it comes to light.

30
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,640
In a way, she's protecting you.

31
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:54,080
Besides, shouldn't you
be pleased that she knows

32
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:57,200
how to conduct herself at work?
Why are you so bothered?

33
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,080
She made a mistake at work.

34
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:04,360
I criticized her,

35
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:06,400
and she still won't talk to me.

36
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,400
There it is.

37
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:17,480
You took the scenic route

38
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,560
to get to the point.

39
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:21,440
Did you make it up to her afterward?

40
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:25,320
Other big-shot bosses
protect their girlfriends.

41
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:26,680
But you?

42
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:29,320
All stick and no carrot.

43
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:32,200
What's she getting
out of this relationship?

44
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:36,200
You don't get it.

45
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:38,720
If she wants to grow quickly at work,

46
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:40,360
she has to solve problems herself.

47
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:43,720
She understands
that this is how she'll learn.

48
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:45,960
And this time,

49
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:47,880
she handled it pretty well.

50
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:49,960
But she was too naive.

51
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:54,640
She thought being loyal at work
would earn her loyalty in return.

52
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:57,320
Foolish.

53
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,840
You just said yourself

54
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:03,160
that she did some things well.

55
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:07,040
Everyone makes mistakes.
Just soften a little.

56
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:09,000
How about this?

57
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,640
Forget the gifts.

58
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:13,000
But starting tomorrow,
send her flowers to show you're sorry.

59
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:14,720
I did nothing wrong.

60
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,440
Why should I send flowers?

61
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:18,760
It's not like anything serious
happened between you two.

62
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:20,360
Why does it matter who's right or wrong?

63
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:23,000
If you want this relationship to work,

64
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,880
send her flowers and smooth things over.

65
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:35,280
Will flowers really work?

66
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:37,640
Of course.

67
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:40,000
Women go weak at the knees for flowers.

68
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:41,720
I'll arrange it.

69
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,160
Starting tomorrow, she'll get flowers

70
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:46,040
until she's no longer mad.

71
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:59,080
- Hello. I'm here to see Mr. Luan.
- Just go straight ahead.

72
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:00,840
Please sign here.

73
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:05,800
I've got some gossip.

74
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:11,000
Boss has quietly set up a love nest.

75
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:14,440
Huh?

76
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:15,560
With whom?

77
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:17,720
Her. Look.

78
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:31,960
<i>Luan Nian!</i>

79
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:40,160
Boss rented my grandmother's
courtyard house in the hutong.

80
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:41,280
When I went to hand over the keys,

81
00:06:41,880 --> 00:06:43,400
this gorgeous woman was staying there.

82
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:46,520
Her name is Zang Yao.
She's Luke's childhood friend.

83
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:50,400
The classic childhood sweetheart.

84
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:52,240
Hold on.

85
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:56,400
Look how elegant she is.

86
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:58,800
You can tell at a glance
she and Luke move in the same circles.

87
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:00,040
Look.

88
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,800
Look at this huge cake.

89
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:05,000
She ordered it from Paris

90
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:07,080
for Luke's birthday three years ago.

91
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,440
I picked it up.

92
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:11,360
Back then, she was still studying abroad.

93
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:14,600
This time, Boss specifically said

94
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:19,280
the house had to be nice and quiet,
and he didn't even haggle over the rent.

95
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:22,080
Do you think they're really dating?

96
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:26,520
If they are,
that's quite something for him.

97
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:31,920
Can you imagine
what a man like him will be like

98
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:33,840
when he's in love?

99
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:35,560
That's nice.

100
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:38,280
I still have a report to finish.

101
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:40,200
I'd better get back to it.

102
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,320
Look at that cake.

103
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,160
Lumi, these flowers are for Mr. Luan.

104
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:57,600
Something's definitely up.

105
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:02,440
Weren't we meeting
at Tan Mian's restaurant?

106
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:07,040
I'm almost off work.
Why did you come here?

107
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:09,480
To pick you up.

108
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:11,760
And let you ride in my new car.

109
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:15,080
You just got back.
Where did you get a car?

110
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:16,760
You rented me the house,

111
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,600
and Song and the others arranged the car.

112
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:22,800
Come in.

113
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:30,640
Mr. Luan, your flowers.

114
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:34,360
Is this the surprise
you prepared for me tonight?

115
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:35,679
They're beautiful.

116
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:39,919
Lumi.

117
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:50,320
Should I close the door, Mr. Luan?

118
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:52,400
Thanks.

119
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:00,320
LUAN NIAN

120
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:01,440
<i>Have you left?</i>

121
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:40,480
Tao.

122
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:46,680
Get in. I'm driving everyone home.

123
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:54,480
FATED FOR YOU

124
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,840
Sun Yu,

125
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:00,720
your company's so stingy.

126
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,520
Such a big matchmaking event,

127
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:04,280
and this beat-up
little van delivers the flowers.

128
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:06,240
No wonder they say
poverty makes marriage miserable.

129
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:08,480
If your members
see flowers arriving in this wreck,

130
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:09,800
their dates won't stand a chance.

131
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:12,760
I did my best
to uphold the company's image.

132
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:14,480
Can't you see how nicely I decorated it?

133
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:16,920
I'm just a beggar here,
and beggars can't be choosers.

134
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,520
It's fine. I think it's perfectly fine.

135
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:22,120
You know what?
I bought those flowers wholesale.

136
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:24,680
I'll pick out some nice ones
and put them in our place.

137
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:26,920
Sun Yu.

138
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:30,520
Could you give me a bouquet?

139
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:33,400
Of course. We've got plenty.

140
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:42,040
Cheer up. It's just a bouquet.
I'll give you one.

141
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,360
Tell me what kind you want.

142
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:44,600
I'll send it to your office tomorrow.

143
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:45,680
You'll see a huge bouquet

144
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:48,000
right in the middle of your desk.

145
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:49,280
- How's that?
- Great.

146
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:50,840
What are you two doing?

147
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:52,680
Am I invisible?

148
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:55,000
You're sending her flowers? I'll do it.

149
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:57,080
A different bouquet every day for a week.

150
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,800
I'll outdo everyone at your office.

151
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:01,640
With me around,
you'll get flowers every day.

152
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:02,840
Homegrown and hand-delivered.

153
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:07,240
- What are you talking about?
- A wise man once told me

154
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:09,920
that if no one sends a girl flowers,
it means she has a special quality.

155
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,000
What's that?

156
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:13,400
She's naturally fragrant.

157
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:16,720
Take a good sniff. What do you smell?

158
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,440
What?

159
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:20,440
- Flowers?
- Wrong!

160
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:21,520
Peaches!

161
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:26,520
- Right, peaches, Tao's fragrance.
- Keep your eyes on the road.

162
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:32,040
FATED FOR YOU

163
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,360
Flora, these are for you.

164
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,720
- Thank you.
- No problem.

165
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:52,720
Flora,

166
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:55,000
- are you seeing someone?
- No.

167
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:58,680
White lisianthus
symbolizes everlasting love.

168
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:01,200
Your boyfriend is quite a romantic.

169
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:02,160
Congratulations.

170
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,240
- I don't have one.
- Who sent them?

171
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:05,520
- Morning, Mr. Luan.
- Morning, Mr. Luan.

172
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:18,960
HOPE THIS BRIGHTENS YOUR DAY

173
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:23,680
<i>I got the flowers.</i>

174
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:24,800
<i>Thanks, Lei.</i>

175
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:26,120
SUNFLOWER FAMILY

176
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,280
<i>I haven't sent anything yet.</i>

177
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:28,720
<i>You haven't given me your address.</i>

178
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:30,880
<i>I didn't send them either.</i>

179
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,840
<i>Was it Yuanzhu?</i>

180
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:34,120
<i>Not me either.</i>

181
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:38,240
<i>Looks like Tao has plenty of admirers.</i>

182
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:40,280
<i>We should look into it.</i>

183
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:42,200
<i>Love is in the air.</i>

184
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:05,000
Here. Your flowers.

185
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:07,000
Five days in a row.

186
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:08,560
Will this ever end?

187
00:13:08,640 --> 00:13:09,960
I just went through a breakup.

188
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:13,200
What happened?

189
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:16,560
He's always flirting around.
I caught him red-handed.

190
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:19,360
He sent the exact same gift to two women.

191
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:21,160
Of course,

192
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,760
I dumped him.

193
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:26,040
And now I have to watch you
get flowers every day. I can't take it.

194
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:28,560
Lumi.

195
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:32,360
Does the copy you submitted today
even make sense?

196
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:33,520
Go fix it.

197
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:37,080
The client needs it tomorrow.

198
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:43,040
It's still early. Sneaking out already?

199
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:46,960
No.

200
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:50,080
I cleared it with Alex and Lumi.

201
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:51,360
I'm leaving early.

202
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:54,360
Where are you going?

203
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:57,440
Hiking with some friends.

204
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:01,880
Today's Friday.

205
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:06,400
I know.

206
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,960
We won't be back until Sunday.

207
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:14,240
Have fun.

208
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:16,840
Nice flowers.

209
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:19,560
But they don't suit you.

210
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:23,920
Then what flowers do you think suit me?

211
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,400
Green foxtail.

212
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:48,760
Let's go.

213
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:53,120
What's wrong? You got flowers,
but you still seem down.

214
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:55,480
- You can have them.
- Me?

215
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:39,720
Watch your step, everyone.

216
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:43,880
Keep up.

217
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:46,960
- Let's hit the restroom.
- All right.

218
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:49,400
Want water? I'll get several bottles.

219
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:50,960
- Yes.
- OK.

220
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:52,320
Hurry. I can't hold it much longer.

221
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:56,480
Could the flowers be from Luan Nian?

222
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:57,800
No way.

223
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:59,760
He doesn't think I deserve flowers.

224
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:01,560
Don't put yourself down like that.

225
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:03,720
How many times have I told you?

226
00:16:06,680 --> 00:16:11,720
I wanted flowers because he gave
someone else flowers, and I got jealous.

227
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:20,800
But I feel so silly,
comparing myself to her

228
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:22,280
over a bouquet.

229
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:25,840
You're not silly.

230
00:16:26,680 --> 00:16:28,600
Love makes you possessive.

231
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:31,400
If you stopped feeling that way,
it'd mean you didn't love him anymore.

232
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:33,520
Water. Here.

233
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:37,520
Water. Here.

234
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:38,960
Where did you buy it?

235
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:40,200
- Let's go.
- Thanks.

236
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:41,280
Aren't you two using the restroom?

237
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:42,240
- Lei.
- No.

238
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:43,720
- Let's start climbing.
- Come on.

239
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:44,960
There won't be any restrooms up there.

240
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:47,880
It's cold out here.

241
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:52,000
Let me grab your backpack.
I'm getting tired.

242
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:54,360
- You OK?
- Yes.

243
00:17:05,280 --> 00:17:06,880
It looks easier up there.

244
00:17:07,599 --> 00:17:08,520
Come on.

245
00:17:15,119 --> 00:17:17,160
Then what flowers do you think suit me?

246
00:17:18,359 --> 00:17:19,440
Green foxtail.

247
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:39,880
<i>What are your plans for New Year's Eve?</i>

248
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:45,560
<i>Once the designers finalize the proposal,</i>

249
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:47,680
<i>I'll be at the office overseeing</i>

250
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:49,680
<i>the New Year's Eve</i>
<i>and New Year's Day ad launches.</i>

251
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:55,240
<i>Do you have a passport and a snowboard?</i>

252
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:57,920
<i>No.</i>

253
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:02,680
What's wrong? Getting tired?

254
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:05,680
I just wanted a break.

255
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:07,320
How do you have so much stamina?

256
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:09,320
I grew up in the mountains.

257
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:11,480
Climbing was the best entertainment
we had as kids.

258
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:13,120
No wonder.

259
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:18,320
MOM

260
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:22,200
When I was little,
I only got to go hiking on school trips,

261
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:24,720
but before every trip, my dad would worry

262
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:27,200
that I'd fall
and keep telling me to be careful.

263
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:30,160
I can tell you grew up in a happy family.

264
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:32,400
You can tell?

265
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:35,000
You're innocent and cheerful.

266
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:37,120
It's obvious your parents doted on you.

267
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:39,520
They did.

268
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:43,040
I don't think I've ever had
much to complain about.

269
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:47,960
The man who drove you home last time…

270
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:49,320
Is he your boyfriend?

271
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:54,920
Sort of.

272
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:59,560
Why aren't you dating anyone?

273
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:02,720
I'd rather not make some poor girl suffer.

274
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:06,280
What? Why would she suffer?

275
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:09,760
I think anyone who dated you
would be very happy.

276
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,320
Dating isn't important.

277
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:14,920
Being together is what matters.

278
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:17,320
What are you two talking about?

279
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:19,920
Tao, come on. Keep up.

280
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,960
- We're almost there.
- Coming!

281
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:24,680
- Let's go.
- All right.

282
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:27,000
Here.

283
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:28,320
I'll pull you along.

284
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:29,720
- It's all right.
- Come on.

285
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:42,600
<i>I've already talked to Song,</i>
<i>Tan Mian, and the others.</i>

286
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:44,680
<i>How about we go snowboarding</i>
<i>in Northern Europe</i>

287
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:46,880
<i>for our annual trip this year?</i>

288
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:48,080
BEIJING TO ZURICH

289
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:52,080
FLIGHT BOOKING PAGE

290
00:20:08,960 --> 00:20:12,440
The view was worth the wait.

291
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:14,680
It's breathtaking.

292
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:31,400
I could jump
into this sea of clouds right now.

293
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:38,400
You like clouds?

294
00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:50,280
Let's go up there and make a wish.

295
00:20:56,560 --> 00:20:59,880
I hope all my clients find their match.

296
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:00,880
God of Wealth, God of Marriage,

297
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:03,000
please work your magic! Please!

298
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,280
Make me rich.

299
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,880
What did you wish for?

300
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:19,160
I just wished for my career

301
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:20,400
to keep getting better!

302
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:21,920
Great!

303
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:24,000
Let my house go up in value!

304
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:25,440
- Go up!
- Go up!

305
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:27,480
Yuanzhu, what did you wish for?

306
00:21:29,320 --> 00:21:31,760
I'll be traveling
a lot for work after New Year's.

307
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:34,600
I hope my autonomous
driving tests succeed.

308
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:37,120
They definitely will.

309
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:39,440
We worked so hard to get up here.

310
00:21:39,520 --> 00:21:40,360
How about a group photo?

311
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:41,160
- Sure.
- Sounds good.

312
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:41,960
- Come on.
- Come.

313
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:43,200
- Move closer.
- Tao.

314
00:21:43,280 --> 00:21:44,480
Move closer.

315
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:45,640
One, two.

316
00:21:50,840 --> 00:21:51,720
Done.

317
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:52,720
Let me be rich, please.

318
00:21:53,920 --> 00:21:55,360
It's getting pretty cold.

319
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:57,280
Why don't we head down
and find something to eat?

320
00:21:57,360 --> 00:21:58,480
- Sure.
- I looked it up.

321
00:21:58,560 --> 00:22:00,480
The best food around here
is wood-fired chicken.

322
00:22:00,560 --> 00:22:02,120
- I've heard of it.
- Let's go.

323
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:03,280
- Come on.
- Let's go.

324
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:04,200
Yuanzhu's paying.

325
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:05,320
- I'm freezing.
- Is it this way?

326
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:14,840
<i>Today is New Year's Eve.</i>

327
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:18,600
<i>Beijing's evening rush hour</i>
<i>is expected to begin as early as 3 p.m.</i>

328
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:21,360
<i>Please plan ahead if you're heading out.</i>

329
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,800
<i>Public transportation is recommended.</i>

330
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:34,800
- Lumi, I'm leaving. Bye.
- I'm leaving as well.

331
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:36,560
- Happy New Year.
- Happy New Year.

332
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:37,720
Bye, Lumi.

333
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:38,800
Take it easy. Don't drink too much.

334
00:22:42,240 --> 00:22:43,360
Flora,

335
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:46,160
what are your plans for tonight?

336
00:22:46,760 --> 00:22:50,280
I want to sleep all night.
I've been exhausted lately.

337
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:52,160
Boring.

338
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:53,160
I'm heading out, then.

339
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:55,320
Traffic will be gridlocked everywhere.
Get home early.

340
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:56,720
I'll leave once the client replies.

341
00:22:58,600 --> 00:22:59,840
LUAN NIAN: EVERYONE CAN LEAVE EARLY TODAY

342
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:01,360
No need to wait.

343
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:02,840
Luke's already celebrating
New Year's in Switzerland.

344
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:05,600
Let's go. No one's here
to keep tabs on us.

345
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:07,520
Happy New Year.

346
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:09,200
- Happy New Year.
- Go on. Get going.

347
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:17,560
SWITZERLAND

348
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:19,040
I'm exhausted.

349
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:21,760
The snow's really good this year.

350
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:23,360
- The snow's good.
- I love my new board.

351
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:24,600
But I wasn't at my best today.

352
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:25,680
It's amazing.

353
00:23:25,760 --> 00:23:27,680
You need to practice
your carving next year. Seriously.

354
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:30,080
I'm scared to go too fast. You know?

355
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:31,680
It requires too much speed.

356
00:23:31,760 --> 00:23:33,760
And when you're going downhill,
you need to crouch lower.

357
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:36,840
Come over here. Stop talking.

358
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:38,080
Let's take a group photo.

359
00:23:38,680 --> 00:23:41,800
When we're old and gray,
we can look back on it.

360
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:43,640
- I'll never grow old.
- Old and gray?

361
00:23:43,720 --> 00:23:44,400
I'll never…

362
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:46,160
- Luan Nian, what are you doing?
- Luan Nian.

363
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:47,280
- Luke, photo!
- Look at the camera.

364
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:48,280
Hurry.

365
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:49,400
- Come on.
- Let's take it.

366
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:51,080
One, two, three.

367
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:53,200
- Let me see.
- Let me see.

368
00:23:53,920 --> 00:23:56,000
- I'm so handsome.
- We didn't get him in it.

369
00:23:56,080 --> 00:23:58,160
- You blocked him.
- Let's go.

370
00:23:59,920 --> 00:24:02,880
What are you looking at?
You weren't even in the photo.

371
00:24:02,960 --> 00:24:03,880
Come on.

372
00:24:05,760 --> 00:24:08,080
One, two, three.

373
00:24:10,520 --> 00:24:11,360
- Come on.
- Let's drink.

374
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:12,440
Cheers.

375
00:24:13,040 --> 00:24:14,360
Drink up, everyone.

376
00:24:16,160 --> 00:24:17,040
What's on your mind?

377
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:18,400
You keep sitting here alone.

378
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:21,040
I haven't snowboarded much
these past two years,

379
00:24:21,120 --> 00:24:22,960
so I was really off today.

380
00:24:23,040 --> 00:24:23,880
Want anything? I'll get it for you.

381
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:25,840
No, thanks. You guys eat.

382
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:27,640
- Honestly…
- Don't drink alone. Come join us.

383
00:24:29,560 --> 00:24:30,880
You always have to butt in.

384
00:24:36,760 --> 00:24:37,800
Luke,

385
00:24:38,360 --> 00:24:40,720
why don't you two
finally make it official on this trip?

386
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,000
Have any of your relationships
ever worked out?

387
00:24:51,120 --> 00:24:52,880
Sure.

388
00:24:53,760 --> 00:24:56,320
Just… a few too many times.

389
00:24:57,400 --> 00:24:58,360
With disastrous results.

390
00:24:59,520 --> 00:25:00,840
That's why I'm worried about you.

391
00:25:02,040 --> 00:25:03,080
Yao.

392
00:25:04,360 --> 00:25:07,840
I've always felt like you've been
hiding something these past few years.

393
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:09,720
How about I drink with you tonight,

394
00:25:09,800 --> 00:25:10,840
and you tell me
what's really on your mind?

395
00:25:11,440 --> 00:25:12,680
Cheers.

396
00:25:12,760 --> 00:25:15,320
Any secrets between us stay between us.

397
00:25:15,400 --> 00:25:17,120
Why would I tell you?

398
00:25:19,360 --> 00:25:20,600
All I know is

399
00:25:20,680 --> 00:25:23,400
that we've always
been really close friends.

400
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:26,200
But at the beginning,

401
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:28,480
I don't think either of us
wanted to be just friends.

402
00:25:31,680 --> 00:25:32,520
Come on.

403
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:33,520
Let's drink.

404
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:34,640
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

405
00:25:36,680 --> 00:25:37,720
I have a girlfriend.

406
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:41,280
What?

407
00:25:42,120 --> 00:25:43,680
Wait. You have a girlfriend?

408
00:25:43,760 --> 00:25:44,880
Since when?

409
00:25:45,680 --> 00:25:47,200
Are you serious?

410
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:49,000
And you didn't even tell me?

411
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:50,360
Do we know her?

412
00:25:50,440 --> 00:25:52,680
What's there to announce
about my love life?

413
00:25:53,840 --> 00:25:57,360
That's a pretty feeble excuse
for turning me down.

414
00:26:02,920 --> 00:26:04,120
Come on.

415
00:26:05,760 --> 00:26:06,800
Don't be upset.

416
00:26:06,880 --> 00:26:08,560
You know what Luan Nian's like.

417
00:26:09,160 --> 00:26:10,400
That's just how he talks.

418
00:26:13,840 --> 00:26:15,800
SIMPLY DELICIOUS

419
00:26:15,880 --> 00:26:17,640
What's wrong? What happened?

420
00:26:20,760 --> 00:26:22,120
I ran into my ex.

421
00:26:23,440 --> 00:26:25,720
He was spending
New Year's Eve with his girlfriend.

422
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:27,160
And to make things worse,

423
00:26:28,360 --> 00:26:29,840
a coworker's event went wrong,

424
00:26:30,600 --> 00:26:32,400
and my boss tried
to make me take the blame.

425
00:26:34,080 --> 00:26:35,480
I refused,

426
00:26:35,560 --> 00:26:38,280
so he called me into his office
and chewed me out.

427
00:26:39,200 --> 00:26:41,040
There goes my year-end bonus.

428
00:26:41,920 --> 00:26:44,040
Don't cry, OK?

429
00:26:44,600 --> 00:26:47,600
Don't punish yourself
for other people's mistakes.

430
00:26:47,680 --> 00:26:49,560
Just ignore them.

431
00:26:49,640 --> 00:26:51,120
Don't you always take things in stride?

432
00:26:53,640 --> 00:26:54,840
But Tao,

433
00:26:56,640 --> 00:26:59,800
why is every step here so hard?

434
00:27:04,520 --> 00:27:06,720
We chose this path ourselves.

435
00:27:07,320 --> 00:27:08,600
You know what they say.

436
00:27:08,680 --> 00:27:13,760
Part of your salary
is for putting up with unfair treatment.

437
00:27:14,480 --> 00:27:16,080
And there's an old saying,

438
00:27:16,160 --> 00:27:19,960
if the road feels hard,
it's because we're going uphill.

439
00:27:20,840 --> 00:27:22,440
That means we're making progress,

440
00:27:22,520 --> 00:27:23,440
right?

441
00:27:27,760 --> 00:27:28,840
Right.

442
00:27:29,560 --> 00:27:30,760
Here.

443
00:27:30,840 --> 00:27:32,320
New Year's gifts for you.

444
00:27:34,480 --> 00:27:35,800
It's beautiful.

445
00:27:37,800 --> 00:27:39,080
Thank you.

446
00:27:39,160 --> 00:27:41,880
Oh my gosh. You even got us gifts.

447
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:43,880
Thank you, Yuanzhu.

448
00:27:46,560 --> 00:27:49,960
The world would be a better place
with more people like you.

449
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:53,760
No more bad work.

450
00:27:54,520 --> 00:27:55,960
No more bad men.

451
00:27:57,760 --> 00:27:58,600
Well…

452
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:04,760
There are always
a few truly awful men in the world,

453
00:28:04,840 --> 00:28:05,960
of truly awful men in the world,

454
00:28:06,040 --> 00:28:08,480
and you just happened to meet one of them.

455
00:28:12,720 --> 00:28:14,600
I… I'm not good at comforting people.

456
00:28:15,600 --> 00:28:18,720
How about I treat you to a movie later?

457
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:20,320
OK.

458
00:28:21,120 --> 00:28:22,560
A midnight movie?

459
00:28:23,160 --> 00:28:24,400
I've never been to one.

460
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:25,920
Neither have I.

461
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:26,960
That's a shame.

462
00:28:27,040 --> 00:28:30,520
When I was in school, I was always broke.

463
00:28:30,600 --> 00:28:32,000
So during the holidays,

464
00:28:32,080 --> 00:28:34,920
my classmates and I
would always go to midnight movies.

465
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:36,360
Great. Let's go after dinner.

466
00:28:36,960 --> 00:28:38,320
- OK.
- Great.

467
00:28:40,040 --> 00:28:41,880
It's New Year's Eve.

468
00:28:41,960 --> 00:28:43,280
I should cheer up.

469
00:28:45,240 --> 00:28:46,120
Pull it together.

470
00:28:47,960 --> 00:28:50,000
Let's take a group photo
and send it to Lei.

471
00:28:50,080 --> 00:28:52,600
It'll commemorate
our first New Year's Eve together.

472
00:28:52,680 --> 00:28:54,480
- OK.
- Hold on.

473
00:28:54,560 --> 00:28:56,160
I brought some props.

474
00:28:56,240 --> 00:28:57,240
You brought props?

475
00:28:57,320 --> 00:28:58,520
We need to get into the New Year's spirit.

476
00:28:59,560 --> 00:29:00,400
This one's for you.

477
00:29:01,320 --> 00:29:03,080
- OK.
- And this one's for you.

478
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:06,640
- Do we put them on?
- I'll show you.

479
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:08,120
Put it on,

480
00:29:08,720 --> 00:29:09,920
like this.

481
00:29:12,760 --> 00:29:14,040
So childish. So childish.

482
00:29:26,960 --> 00:29:29,360
Why did you say that?
When did you get a girlfriend?

483
00:29:30,800 --> 00:29:31,720
Go check on her.

484
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:41,560
How was I supposed to know
he had a girlfriend?

485
00:29:46,160 --> 00:29:48,280
Zang Yao, let's talk outside.

486
00:30:07,720 --> 00:30:09,600
Do we have to talk about this
on New Year's Eve?

487
00:30:11,080 --> 00:30:12,440
You know,

488
00:30:12,520 --> 00:30:15,560
this could ruin
every New Year's Eve for me.

489
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:20,680
I don't remember ever expressing
any special feelings for you.

490
00:30:22,680 --> 00:30:24,400
I only wanted us to be family

491
00:30:25,160 --> 00:30:26,240
and best friends.

492
00:30:42,760 --> 00:30:44,120
I got the wrong idea.

493
00:30:47,640 --> 00:30:49,200
I'm sorry if I hurt you.

494
00:30:52,720 --> 00:30:54,000
You don't have to apologize.

495
00:30:54,840 --> 00:30:57,800
You're Luan Nian, after all.
Luan Nian never admits he's wrong.

496
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:12,120
Do you really have a girlfriend?

497
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:17,040
Yes.

498
00:31:22,400 --> 00:31:23,360
All right.

499
00:31:24,080 --> 00:31:25,480
Then I'm happy for you.

500
00:31:29,200 --> 00:31:30,960
I hope I haven't ruined
your New Year's Eve.

501
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:33,320
You haven't.

502
00:31:34,880 --> 00:31:37,960
I don't know why
she isn't here with you today,

503
00:31:39,640 --> 00:31:42,200
but since we're here,
we should enjoy ourselves.

504
00:31:44,560 --> 00:31:45,520
I'm going inside.

505
00:31:55,280 --> 00:31:57,000
Is it almost midnight?

506
00:31:57,080 --> 00:31:57,920
Time for the countdown.

507
00:31:58,680 --> 00:31:59,800
Time for the countdown.

508
00:32:04,440 --> 00:32:05,960
SHANG ZHITAO

509
00:32:09,520 --> 00:32:10,720
Ten.

510
00:32:10,800 --> 00:32:11,640
Nine.

511
00:32:11,720 --> 00:32:12,840
Eight.

512
00:32:12,920 --> 00:32:14,160
Seven.

513
00:32:14,240 --> 00:32:15,800
Six. Five.

514
00:32:16,400 --> 00:32:17,240
Four.

515
00:32:17,320 --> 00:32:18,280
Three.

516
00:32:18,360 --> 00:32:19,280
Two.

517
00:32:19,360 --> 00:32:20,600
One!

518
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:23,200
<i>Happy New Year!</i>

519
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:26,280
Are you out?

520
00:32:27,880 --> 00:32:30,520
I'm celebrating New Year's
with my friends.

521
00:32:31,360 --> 00:32:32,480
<i>Happy New Year.</i>

522
00:32:36,920 --> 00:32:40,560
I hope you and your friends
have a great time.

523
00:32:46,800 --> 00:32:49,640
If you're free tomorrow,
go to my place and check on my fish.

524
00:32:50,560 --> 00:32:51,760
You know the door code.

525
00:32:55,200 --> 00:32:56,400
Sure.

526
00:33:13,360 --> 00:33:15,000
- Happy New Year.
- Cheers.

527
00:33:15,080 --> 00:33:16,040
Happy New Year.

528
00:33:16,120 --> 00:33:18,760
I'm glad I have you guys. Thank you.

529
00:33:19,560 --> 00:33:20,680
Feeling better now?

530
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:26,880
To the New Year!

531
00:33:29,680 --> 00:33:30,880
Do you think

532
00:33:32,400 --> 00:33:34,320
Switzerland is cold?

533
00:33:34,400 --> 00:33:35,240
Switzerland?

534
00:33:36,200 --> 00:33:37,280
It's not too bad.

535
00:33:37,360 --> 00:33:38,840
It has a temperate monsoon climate.

536
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:44,760
Compared with Harbin,
Switzerland is just cool.

537
00:33:45,560 --> 00:33:46,400
Right.

538
00:33:47,880 --> 00:33:50,280
Then I must be a fake Harbin native.

539
00:33:50,360 --> 00:33:51,480
I'm really sensitive to the cold.

540
00:33:51,560 --> 00:33:54,720
Every winter, I wear layer after layer.

541
00:33:54,800 --> 00:33:55,720
That's good.

542
00:33:56,240 --> 00:33:57,480
You know how to keep warm.

543
00:33:59,120 --> 00:33:59,960
Come on.

544
00:34:00,040 --> 00:34:01,160
Happy New Year.

545
00:34:01,240 --> 00:34:02,440
Happy New Year.

546
00:34:21,679 --> 00:34:23,440
BAR

547
00:34:28,159 --> 00:34:30,600
<i>Verified. Please open the door.</i>

548
00:34:36,760 --> 00:34:39,880
Luke, how should I take care of your fish?

549
00:34:40,800 --> 00:34:42,080
<i>Listen carefully and do exactly as I say.</i>

550
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:50,040
<i>Replace the filter pad in the fish tank.</i>

551
00:34:53,719 --> 00:34:55,639
<i>The pads are in the cabinet</i>
<i>under the staghorn fern.</i>

552
00:35:03,680 --> 00:35:05,040
<i>There are gloves in the box.</i>

553
00:35:05,120 --> 00:35:05,960
LUAN NIAN

554
00:35:09,040 --> 00:35:12,440
<i>Open the cabinet under the tank</i>
<i>and find the filter first.</i>

555
00:35:15,520 --> 00:35:17,520
<i>Take out the old filter pad,</i>

556
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:18,680
<i>then put the new one in.</i>

557
00:35:24,240 --> 00:35:25,880
<i>Check the thermometer beside it.</i>

558
00:35:27,200 --> 00:35:29,520
<i>Make sure the water temperature is right,</i>
<i>then add a little fish food.</i>

559
00:35:31,080 --> 00:35:32,200
<i>Luan Nian, come.</i>

560
00:35:33,720 --> 00:35:34,680
<i>Just follow my instructions.</i>

561
00:35:35,440 --> 00:35:36,640
<i>I'm hanging up.</i>

562
00:36:12,120 --> 00:36:14,200
<i>Verified. Please open the door.</i>

563
00:36:38,040 --> 00:36:40,080
<i>I hope you and the fish</i>

564
00:36:40,160 --> 00:36:43,720
<i>get everything you wish for</i>
<i>in the new year.</i>

565
00:36:54,440 --> 00:36:55,480
TAN MIAN

566
00:36:56,880 --> 00:36:57,720
Hello?

567
00:36:57,800 --> 00:36:59,520
<i>Seriously?</i>

568
00:36:59,600 --> 00:37:02,120
<i>We woke up</i>
<i>and were told you'd checked out.</i>

569
00:37:02,200 --> 00:37:03,080
<i>You're back in Beijing?</i>

570
00:37:04,160 --> 00:37:05,280
Yeah.

571
00:37:05,360 --> 00:37:07,600
<i>Did you go to see Ms. Shang?</i>

572
00:37:07,680 --> 00:37:08,800
None of your business.

573
00:38:16,680 --> 00:38:21,080
POSTS ABOUT SWITZERLAND

574
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:31,840
ZANG YAO: VISIT SWITZERLAND
WITH THE PEOPLE YOU LOVE AT LEAST ONCE

575
00:38:31,920 --> 00:38:33,040
GET A LITTLE TIPSY, LOOK AT ONE ANOTHER
AND SAY, "LET'S STAY TOGETHER FOREVER."

576
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:53,120
<i>I…</i>

577
00:38:55,200 --> 00:38:56,200
I'm in a relationship

578
00:38:57,680 --> 00:38:59,080
that isn't right.

579
00:39:00,240 --> 00:39:03,360
I always thought
I didn't care how it'd end

580
00:39:04,360 --> 00:39:10,640
or that I never expected a happy ending.

581
00:39:12,200 --> 00:39:13,840
But that isn't true.

582
00:39:16,720 --> 00:39:17,600
I'm…

583
00:39:18,320 --> 00:39:19,400
I'm awful.

584
00:39:19,480 --> 00:39:20,720
You're not awful.

585
00:39:26,480 --> 00:39:27,600
You're still young.

586
00:39:28,960 --> 00:39:30,680
Being young means you have
the chance to make mistakes.

587
00:39:31,960 --> 00:39:33,640
Never settle for less than you deserve.

588
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:36,840
I believe you have the courage
to break out of your shell.

589
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:39,680
Even if you don't yet,

590
00:39:40,440 --> 00:39:41,760
you will someday.

591
00:40:00,280 --> 00:40:01,760
<i>Shang Zhitao, I'm coming to see you now.</i>

592
00:40:13,240 --> 00:40:17,760
<i>The classic childhood sweetheart.</i>

593
00:40:17,840 --> 00:40:20,280
<i>You can tell at a glance</i>
<i>she and Luke move in the same circles.</i>

594
00:40:20,360 --> 00:40:23,400
<i>Do you think they're really dating?</i>

595
00:40:32,320 --> 00:40:33,840
Aren't you cold dressed like this?

596
00:40:38,320 --> 00:40:39,920
This is from the ski resort.

597
00:40:44,040 --> 00:40:45,080
I don't know how to snowboard.

598
00:40:46,960 --> 00:40:48,040
You can learn.

599
00:40:56,600 --> 00:40:57,920
I've realized…

600
00:41:01,200 --> 00:41:03,160
we're from completely different worlds.

601
00:41:09,400 --> 00:41:11,160
I don't know how to snowboard,

602
00:41:11,240 --> 00:41:13,040
and I don't want to learn for now

603
00:41:13,640 --> 00:41:15,640
because the ski passes are expensive.

604
00:41:16,560 --> 00:41:18,880
And I certainly wouldn't go
to Switzerland just to snowboard.

605
00:41:19,720 --> 00:41:23,280
Sorry to let
such an expensive gift go to waste.

606
00:41:28,160 --> 00:41:30,600
Are you still upset
about what happened at work?

607
00:41:32,120 --> 00:41:36,000
Didn't you say we should keep things
strictly professional at work?

608
00:41:36,600 --> 00:41:38,800
If you're unhappy with the way
I handled it, you can talk to me.

609
00:41:38,880 --> 00:41:41,000
Why bring it into our relationship?

610
00:41:42,680 --> 00:41:44,400
This isn't about work.

611
00:41:48,560 --> 00:41:49,920
You said before

612
00:41:51,200 --> 00:41:53,960
that if either of us
stopped liking the other,

613
00:41:54,040 --> 00:41:55,360
we could end things.

614
00:42:01,200 --> 00:42:02,480
Is there someone else?

615
00:42:03,240 --> 00:42:04,240
No.

616
00:42:04,320 --> 00:42:06,080
Then what do you mean? Just say it.

617
00:42:08,160 --> 00:42:09,400
I mean,

618
00:42:10,240 --> 00:42:12,920
if you start seeing someone else,
you have to tell me.

619
00:42:16,560 --> 00:42:18,320
You must be delusional.

620
00:42:18,400 --> 00:42:20,040
Do you think I sleep
with someone everywhere I go?

621
00:42:20,120 --> 00:42:22,160
Do you think every woman
I meet is after me?

622
00:43:01,520 --> 00:43:02,880
Are you all right?

623
00:43:02,960 --> 00:43:04,040
Let me see.

624
00:43:06,280 --> 00:43:08,440
Good grief. Your forehead's
hot enough to fry an egg.

625
00:43:08,520 --> 00:43:09,800
You have a fever.

626
00:43:11,480 --> 00:43:12,920
I do feel a little warm.

627
00:43:15,520 --> 00:43:16,640
Go home right now.
Why are you still working?

628
00:43:16,720 --> 00:43:18,560
- Go.
- I haven't filed for sick leave yet.

629
00:43:18,640 --> 00:43:19,920
Don't worry about it.

630
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:22,640
I've got a stack of sick leave forms
in my drawer. Go home.

631
00:43:54,880 --> 00:43:57,040
LUAN NIAN

632
00:44:10,200 --> 00:44:12,120
<i>Lumi says you have a fever.</i>

633
00:44:12,640 --> 00:44:13,800
<i>Is it bad?</i>

634
00:44:13,880 --> 00:44:14,920
<i>Have you been to the hospital?</i>

635
00:44:15,520 --> 00:44:17,400
<i>Do you want me to come over now?</i>

636
00:44:17,480 --> 00:44:18,600
<i>Answer me.</i>

637
00:44:26,040 --> 00:44:28,040
LUAN NIAN

638
00:44:32,960 --> 00:44:34,000
<i>Open the door.</i>

639
00:45:08,320 --> 00:45:09,360
Don't take pictures.

640
00:45:10,040 --> 00:45:11,000
These aren't for you.

641
00:45:11,600 --> 00:45:13,360
I don't care who they're for.

642
00:45:13,440 --> 00:45:14,440
First come, first served.

643
00:45:15,880 --> 00:45:18,160
There isn't a love letter
in here, is there?

644
00:45:20,560 --> 00:45:22,400
Buy your own if you like them.

645
00:45:24,880 --> 00:45:27,120
You're no fun.

646
00:45:27,200 --> 00:45:28,680
It's just a bouquet.

647
00:45:29,280 --> 00:45:31,280
If I take it,
you can just buy another one.

648
00:45:32,240 --> 00:45:35,320
And here I was planning to invite you over
for a housewarming dinner tonight.

649
00:45:36,280 --> 00:45:37,800
I just learned on my phone

650
00:45:37,880 --> 00:45:40,000
how to make egg fried rice.

651
00:45:40,080 --> 00:45:41,920
I was going to show off my skills.

652
00:45:42,000 --> 00:45:44,720
Go to Tan Mian's restaurant
if you want something to eat.

653
00:45:44,800 --> 00:45:47,480
If you burn down the courtyard house,
I can't afford to pay for it.

654
00:45:49,800 --> 00:45:51,360
You'd even cover the damages for me?

655
00:45:52,680 --> 00:45:53,920
That alone proves

656
00:45:54,000 --> 00:45:57,040
all these years of friendship
weren't for nothing.

657
00:45:57,640 --> 00:45:58,640
By the way,

658
00:45:58,720 --> 00:46:01,320
I've talked to Song, Tan Mian,
and the others.

659
00:46:01,400 --> 00:46:05,160
How about we take
our annual trip over New Year's

660
00:46:05,240 --> 00:46:07,080
and go snowboarding in Northern Europe?

661
00:46:08,360 --> 00:46:10,720
I've already set the dates.
You can't miss it.

662
00:46:13,880 --> 00:46:16,760
You won't have that much work
over New Year's, will you?

663
00:46:19,560 --> 00:46:20,400
We'll see.

664
00:46:21,480 --> 00:46:23,640
No. You have to come.

665
00:46:26,120 --> 00:46:27,280
It's almost time.

666
00:46:28,640 --> 00:46:30,880
Get ready. We should go.

667
00:46:30,960 --> 00:46:32,280
I'm going to the restroom.

668
00:46:43,600 --> 00:46:46,400
TO SHANG ZHITAO: HAVE YOU LEFT?
